menu "TrailCamHub: schedule"

config SCHEDULE_CAMERA_PLAN
    string "Camera read plan"
    default "*=120"
    help
        Applies on battery power, or when the hub pushes to a configured
        destination; otherwise (mains, nothing to push to) there are no
        automatic reads unless camera_plan is set.
        When the hub reads the cameras on its own: time windows in local time
        (TIME_ZONE), each with an interval in minutes, and "*" for the rest
        of the day, for example
          05:00-09:00=30,17:00-22:00=30,*=120
        reads every 30 minutes at dawn and dusk and every two hours
        otherwise. An interval of 0 means no reads; an empty plan or "off"
        means no automatic reads at all. The first window that contains a
        time applies. Without a valid clock the windows are ignored and the
        "*" interval applies (if it is 0 or missing, the longest window
        interval). Each read wakes the camera's Wi-Fi for a minute or two,
        which costs its battery. A read is followed by a backend sync if the
        uplink is configured.
        Overridden by "config set camera_plan" (serial console, web
        installer) and by the backend.

config SCHEDULE_QUIET
    string "Quiet hours (local time)"
    default "23:00-06:00"
    help
        Applies on battery power; on mains there are no quiet hours unless
        "quiet" is set. A time window "HH:MM-HH:MM" in local time
        (TIME_ZONE), which may span midnight. Inside it the hub neither
        reads the cameras nor checks in and sleeps until the end; what was
        due waits and runs at the end (a read, which also syncs). A read
        asked for by the app waits as well. The BOOT button and a power-on
        still start a cycle. "off" or an empty text: no quiet hours. Needs
        a valid clock, otherwise it is ignored.
        Overridden by "config set quiet".

config SCHEDULE_LOCATION
    string "Location of the hub (LAT,LON in decimal degrees)"
    default ""
    help
        For the sun times of read windows such as
        "sunrise-60..sunrise+90=30" in the camera plan, for example
        "52.5,13.4" (rounded to 0.1 degrees, about 10 km). Empty: the
        hub uses the middle of Germany (51.0,10.0), which is off by up to
        about 25 minutes at the borders, and tells it in "status".
        Overridden by "config set location".

config SCHEDULE_ENERGY
    bool "Check in more often when the battery history allows it"
    default y
    help
        The hub keeps the charge of its cell in the morning and how long the
        cell sat full while charging for the last seven days (needs the
        battery gauge). A cell that is well charged in the morning with a
        steady trend shortens the check-in interval in steps (x0.75, x0.5);
        a low morning or a falling trend take it back. A full cell halves it
        at once for the rest of the day. Camera reads are not affected.
        Not at a low or critical hub battery. See docs/power-and-schedule.md.

config SCHEDULE_ENERGY_TARGET_PERCENT
    int "Charge the cell should have in the morning (%)"
    depends on SCHEDULE_ENERGY
    range 20 90
    default 60

config SCHEDULE_MIN_INTERVAL_MIN
    int "Shortest check-in interval with the energy factor (minutes)"
    depends on SCHEDULE_ENERGY
    range 5 120
    default 10

config SCHEDULE_CHECKIN_INTERVAL_MIN
    int "Backend check-in interval (minutes, 0 = off)"
    range 0 1440
    default 30
    help
        Applies when the hub pushes (direction push); with pull there are no
        check-ins.
        How often the hub syncs with the backend between camera reads, to
        pick up commands from the app (for example a camera read on
        request) and upload what is left. Only with complete uplink
        settings; every camera read syncs as well and restarts the
        interval. Overridden by "config set checkin_min" and by the
        backend.

config SCHEDULE_START_DELAY_S
    int "Delay before the first scheduled cycle after power-on (seconds)"
    range 0 3600
    default 60
    help
        Gives the web installer and the serial console time before the
        first automatic camera read or check-in after a power-on or reset.
        Not applied after a wake-up from deep sleep.

config SCHEDULE_LOW_BATTERY_PERCENT
    int "Camera battery level that stretches the read interval (%, 0 = off)"
    range 0 100
    default 20

config SCHEDULE_LOW_BATTERY_FACTOR
    int "Read interval factor for a camera with a low battery"
    range 1 16
    default 3
    help
        Failed reads stretch the interval as well (2, 4, 8, 16 times after
        one to four failures in a row), and failed check-ins stretch the
        check-in interval in the same way, up to one day.

endmenu
